# /etc/liquidity-migration/bybit-mainnet-attestor.env -- root:root, mode 0600
#
# Operator-owned, read-only funded-account attestation capability. Copy this
# file to the path above and fill all four values before a funded rollout.
# Create a separate Bybit key on the dedicated engine UID. Bybit must report it
# as globally read-only, UTA-bound, created on or after 2026-08-27T22:30:00Z,
# and allowlisted only to the one VPS address recorded below. It needs the
# ContractTrade Order and Position query scopes plus Wallet AccountTransfer
# query scope; global read-only must prevent order, position, or transfer
# mutation, and Wallet Withdraw must be absent.
#
# The deployed engine service never loads this file. Only rollout proofs and
# transient `attest-flat` and stopped-engine `loss-reset` controls receive it
# through systemd EnvironmentFile. Do not add REAL_MONEY, the write key, Telegram
# values, or any other assignment: rollout and ops require a regular root:root
# mode-0600 file and validate exactly these four non-empty assignments.

BYBIT_ATTEST_API_KEY=
BYBIT_ATTEST_API_SECRET=
BYBIT_ATTEST_API_KEY_IP=
BYBIT_ENGINE_EXCLUSIVE_ACCOUNT_USER_ID=
